Build emits dist/assets/logo-*.svg (not inlined). Typecheck PASS, contrast PASS.

Check that the built HTML references ./assets/... and CSP img-src 'self' allows it. Relative path from dist/index.html → ./assets/logo-...svg, same origin for file://? For file:// protocol, 'self' matching in Chromium... hmm! With file:// loading, `img-src 'self'` — does 'self' cover file:// URLs? Chromium treats file:// origin as opaque; CSP 'self' with file: may block. But note the layout test runs the built app and screenshots home; if the image is blocked, the test will surface it (I'm adding a visibility assertion with naturalWidth>0).

Let me add that assertion: check `naturalWidth > 0` (catches CSP block, which renders a broken image with naturalWidth 0).

Now update layout.test.mjs:
- Before clicking Skip: assert brand mark visible on the startup screen.
- In the width loop: assert brand mark visible with natural size > 0; at widths ≥960 assert the tile is visible; at 640 assert tile hidden (per media query) — hmm, asserting hidden locks in a design choice; the plan says tile on Home and check "render at 960, 1440, and narrow widths". Assert: mark visible at all widths; tile visible ≥960; no overflow at all widths (existing).
- Normal motion: transition-duration > 0.
- Reduced motion: transition-duration 0, hover doesn't move.

Careful: the existing test at line 109 sets emulateMedia reducedMotion at the end while on Home at 1100. Also the `--motion-*` assertions.

Where to add the normal-motion transition check? Right after the tab-order assertions at 1100, before clicking "Start a session" (line 90) or after returning Home (line 101). After line 101 the page is Home. Then keyboard '?' test, then reduced motion. I'll add after line 101 (Home, 1100):

```js
const tileTransition = await page.evaluate(() =>
  getComputedStyle(document.querySelector('.board-tile-face')).transitionDuration
);
assert.ok(Number.parseFloat(tileTransition) > 0, ...);
```

Then in reduced-motion block, extend the evaluate to also read tile transform + transition, hover, compare.

Implementation in reduced block:

```js
await page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'reduce' });
const tile = await page.evaluate(() => {
  const face = document.querySelector('.board-tile-face');
  return {
    transform: face ? getComputedStyle(face).transform : '',
    transition: face ? getComputedStyle(face).transitionDuration : '',
  };
});
assert.notEqual(tile.transform, '', 'the board tile is missing');
assert.equal(Number.parseFloat(tile.transition), 0, `board tile transition is ${tile.transition}`);
await page.hover('.board-tile');
const hovered = await page.evaluate(() => getComputedStyle(document.querySelector('.board-tile-face')).transform);
assert.equal(hovered, tile.transform, 'the board tile moved under reduced motion');
```

Note: getComputedStyle transform returns matrix3d(...) string; equality is exact for the same computed value. Under reduced motion, hover rule sets the same rotate values → same matrix → equal. Good.

Wait: hover on `.board-tile` — the parent div with perspective; hovering the face works too.

Also mouse position: after hover, later assertions? The reduced-motion block is last except app close. But `page.hover` leaves cursor there; fine.

Careful: transform computed for `rotateX(16deg) rotateZ(-6deg)` returns a matrix3d string, deterministic.

