content.text:
Generic `.state-pass`/`.state-fail` only used by framing rows currently (grep in tsx showed none? The grep output only styles.css lines — because `<FramingRow>` used `check-state state-${state}` template literal, not literal "state-pass"). So template strings.

If I put `state-${state}` on the li, the whole li's text turns green/amber. Avoid: use `data-state={state}` on the li instead of a class, and CSS `[data-state='pass'] .check-dot { background: var(--ok) }`. Then `.check-state state-pass` keeps its text colour.

Good: `<li className="framing-check" data-state={state}>`.

Now the game card CSS replacing `.slot-meta` styles:
```css
.game-card {
  margin-bottom: var(--sp-3);
  padding: var(--sp-3);
  border: var(--border-w) solid var(--line);
  border-radius: var(--r-control);
  background: var(--bg);
}
.game-card-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--sp-2); }
.game-card-players { color: var(--text); font-size: var(--fs-sm); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.game-card-result { color: var(--text); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
.game-facts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-4); margin: var(--sp-2) 0 0; }
.game-fact { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
.game-fact dt { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.game-fact dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-xs); }
.fact-ok { color: var(--ok); }
.fact-warn { color: var(--warn); }
```
Note: `.game-fact dd` color text, `.fact-warn` overrides to warn — rule order matters; `.fact-warn` after `.game-fact dd` wins by specificity? `.game-fact dd` = 0,1,1; `.fact-warn` = 0,1,0 → `.game-fact dd` wins! Bad. Use `.game-fact dd.fact-warn` / `.game-fact dd.fact-ok`.

Also keep `.meta-excluded` (still used).

Remove `.slot-meta`, `.meta-players`, `.meta-detail`? `.meta-players`/`.meta-detail` no longer used; remove them to avoid dead CSS. `.meta-excluded` kept.

Also `.paste-hint`:
```css
.paste-hint {
  margin-top: var(--sp-2);
  padding: 10px 12px;
  border-left: 3px solid var(--pulse);
  border-radius: var(--r-control);
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}
```
Hmm `p` max-width 36rem is fine.

